def dedupe(items):
    return list(dict.fromkeys(items))


def dedupe_by(items, key):
    seen = set()
    out = []
    for item in items:
        k = key(item)
        if k not in seen:
            seen.add(k)
            out.append(item)
    return out
```
Both make exactly one pass, so a generator is consumed once, and neither compares items for ordering.
